{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:32:16.571Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary:\n\n## What I did\n\n**Added `src/core/web/system-graph-trace.ts`** (`buildSystemGraphTrace`, 248 lines): builds the traceability half of the system graph for opted-in capabilities — `test`/`function` nodes; `owns`, `proves`, `covers`, `serves`, `follows` edges; function `survivors` (from `collectMutationScores`, deduped per `<file>#<function>`); and the `untested`/`unclaimed` gaps, with `sameAdrNumber` matching ADR tags.\n\n**Extended `src/core/web/system-graph-types.ts`** with `SystemGraphTracePart`, `SystemGraphTraceInput`, and `SystemGraphNodeSet<T>`.\n\n**Wired `getSystemGraph`** to build the import graph and scenario index per call, read active/archived changes, collect mutation scores, run the trace builder, and apply its `traceability`/`gaps`/scenario gaps.\n\n**Added `tests/web-system-graph-trace.test.ts`** (250 lines) covering all five \"System graph traceability\" scenarios plus the two \"System graph gaps\" scenarios.\n\n## Verification\n- Task verify: `node --import tsx --test tests/web-system-graph-trace.test.ts` → 7/7 pass.\n- Proposal verify: `pnpm verify` → exit 0 (2606 + 94 tests pass, lint clean).\n\n## Documented deviation\nThe acceptance line asking `getSystemGraph` to share **one** import graph with the code part is only partially met: the traceability side shares the graph built in `getSystemGraph`, but `buildSystemGraphCode` builds its own because `system-graph-code.ts` was not in this task's `scope`. This is recorded under `## Deviated` / `## Missing context` in the result file.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/106-capability-graph/.run/results/3.md`."}}
